The enterprise-licensed component (the litellm-enterprise package, which pip
installs as a dependency of LiteLLM's "proxy" extra) is REMOVED during the
build, because that licence does not permit redistribution. This image
therefore contains only MIT-licensed LiteLLM code, and the enterprise-only
features are absent; they require a subscription from BerriAI in any case.

logo.png is LiteLLM's logo, taken from that repository
(ui/litellm-dashboard/public/assets/logos/litellm_logo.jpg) and resized.
media/screenshot.png is a capture of the LiteLLM admin interface produced by
running this package.

"LiteLLM" and the LiteLLM logo are marks of BerriAI. They are used here only to
identify the software being packaged. This package is not produced, endorsed or
supported by BerriAI; please report packaging problems to this repository and
LiteLLM problems upstream.

The image is not wholly MIT. Beyond LiteLLM it contains that project's Python
dependencies and an Ubuntu base, whose licences include Apache-2.0, MPL-2.0
(certifi, orjson, tqdm), LGPL-2.1 (the libsndfile shared library that arrives
with soundfile) and GPL-3.0-with-GCC-exception (libgfortran and libquadmath,
which arrive with numpy). Each distribution carries its own licence text
inside the image, under its .dist-info directory.

